## Quick start

1. Copy secrets into place (never commit this file):
   ```sh
   cp config/config.example.h config/config.h
   # edit WIFI_SSID / WIFI_PASS / MQTT_* in config/config.h
   ```
2. Wire the device per [WIRING.md](WIRING.md) (`wiring.svg` for a diagram).
3. Validate + compile:
   ```sh
   aiot-sdk test      # full pipeline: static checks, compile, protocol + simulator tests
   aiot-sdk build     # compile only
   ```
4. Flash:
   ```sh
   aiot-sdk flash --port /dev/ttyUSB0
   ```
5. Watch the boot log at 115200 baud; every line starts with `[AIOT]`.

## Project layout

| Path | What |
|------|------|
| `main.ino` | Sketch: wires sensors/actuators into the runtime |
| `AIoT.h` / `AIoT.cpp` | Device runtime (state machine, MQTT, JSON, queue, watchdog) |
| `adapters/` | Sensor adapters (analog, digital, DHT22) |
| `config/aiot.config.json` | Generator input (no secrets — safe to commit) |
| `config/config.h` | Real secrets (**gitignored**) |
| `config/config.example.h` | Template for `config.h` |
| `manifest.json` | Canonical capability manifest (validated by `DeviceManifestSchema`) |
| `manifest_json.h` | Same manifest, embedded in firmware for the retained publish |
| `sketch.yaml` | arduino-cli profile with pinned core/library versions |
| `pinout.json` / `wiring.svg` | Machine-readable pins + wiring diagram |
| `TESTING.md` | How to test this device |

## MQTT topics

All topics live under `aiot/v1/<%= orgId %>/<%= projectId %>/<%= deviceId %>/`:

- `manifest` — retained capability manifest
- `status` — lifecycle state (`BOOT … ONLINE`, `OFFLINE`, `RECONNECTING`)
- `telemetry` — sensor readings
- `command` — commands in, `kind:"result"` replies out
- `presence` — retained online/offline (LWT)
- `health` — 30 s heartbeat

See [TESTING.md](TESTING.md) for the test pipeline and publish gate.
